# ============================================================================
# versions.env - Shared version pins for core.sh and hypr_plugins.sh
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single source of truth for the Hyprland / hyprexpo version pair. Sourced by
# both scripts. Values already present in the environment win (each line uses
# the `: "${VAR:=...}"` pattern), so you can override ad hoc:
#
#   HYPREXPO_REV=v0.55.4 ./hypr_plugins.sh --install
#
# VARIABLES
# ---------
# HYPRLAND_EVR  Exact EVR (version-release) of the hyprland / hyprland-devel
#               packages to install from the lionheartp COPR.
#               Set empty ("") to install whatever is currently latest.
#               Check availability with:  dnf list --showduplicates hyprland
#               NOTE: the COPR only keeps the newest build in its repodata,
#               so an old EVR disappears once a newer build is pushed. On a
#               fresh machine where the pin is gone, core.sh falls back to
#               the latest build with a warning (the hybrid contract).
#
# HYPREXPO_REV  Git tag (or commit) of sandwichfarm/hyprexpo to install.
#               Tags follow "v<hyprland-version>[+N]", e.g. v0.56.2+3.
#               Set empty ("") to auto-resolve the newest tag matching the
#               installed Hyprland version via `git ls-remote` (needs network).
#               When set, hypr_plugins.sh verifies it matches the installed
#               Hyprland version and aborts on drift.
#               hyprpm stores the rev and re-checks-out it on every
#               `hyprpm update`, so the pin sticks across updates.
#
# VERSIONLOCK   1 = after installing, lock hyprland + hyprland-devel to the
#               installed EVR with `dnf5 versionlock` so routine upgrades
#               cannot break the plugin ABI. 0 = skip locking.
#
# BUMP WORKFLOW (update both pins together)
# ----------------------------------------
#   1. sudo dnf versionlock delete hyprland hyprland-devel
#   2. sudo dnf upgrade hyprland hyprland-devel
#   3. Check hyprexpo has a tag for the new version:
#        git ls-remote --tags --refs https://github.com/sandwichfarm/hyprexpo
#   4. Edit HYPRLAND_EVR and HYPREXPO_REV below to match.
#   5. ./hypr_plugins.sh --install --force
#   6. sudo dnf versionlock add hyprland hyprland-devel   (if VERSIONLOCK=1)
# ============================================================================

: "${HYPRLAND_EVR:=0.56.2-3.fc44}"
: "${HYPREXPO_REV:=}"
: "${VERSIONLOCK:=1}"
